jitLLM adaptations of the pinned GGML sources (D-053, D-077), active only
when GGML_JITLLM is defined (third_party/patches/ggml/0002-jitllm-build.patch
defines it):

- ggml.c: ggml_print_backtrace does nothing, so ggml_abort prints its
  message and aborts without forking or executing a debugger.
- ggml-cuda/common.cuh: ggml_cuda_error is not [[noreturn]]. jitLLM defines
  it (src/kernels/ggml/) to record the failure and return, so a launcher
  returns and its caller reports the error instead of the process aborting.
- ggml-cuda/common.cuh: kernel launches use programmatic dependent launch
  as the build decides, without reading GGML_CUDA_PDL from the environment.
- ggml-cuda/common.cuh, top-k.cu: no CUB (GGML_CUDA_USE_CUB stays
  undefined), which jitLLM's license policy does not yet admit for direct
  use (docs/licensing.md): argsort takes its bitonic kernel, and top_k the
  radix select upstream builds for HIP for rows over 1,024, else the
  bitonic argsort.
- ggml-cuda/mmq.cu: the type switch has a case only for the types whose MMQ
  instance units the build compiles, each named by a GGML_JITLLM_MMQ_<type>
  definition, so the other instances are not linked.
- ggml-cuda/mmq.cu, mmvq.cu: a weight tensor without a backend buffer (all
  of jitLLM's) skips the compute-buffer padding clear, which would otherwise
  assert on the missing buffer.

